  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A Uniform rod <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is hinged at its end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and the other end of the rod is connected to a block through a massless string as shown in the figure. The pulley is smooth and massless. Masses of the block and the rod are same and are equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>. The&nbsp;acceleration of the block just after the release from this position is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-05-23_at_8.46.38_PM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 188px;\" /></p>\r",
